Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 00:23:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09868/11362] Fix what the adversarial review of
 REQ-ARC-WMTE-6710 found

An independent hostile review of 288ea485f9 found that commit shipped TWO RED
tests and one real bug. Its "82 tests pass across the 7 affected suites" line was
true of the seven suites I chose and false of the repository. The suite set was
narrower than the concept it named -- this project's own named bug class,
committed inside a commit about that bug class.

THE TWO RED TESTS.

- tests/python/test_experiment_4544_llm_proposer_reinduction.py asserted the
  exception path reports `no_reachable_plan_after_refinement`. That assertion
  pinned the defect REQ-6710 removes, and its very next line asserted the
  counterexample kind IS the exception -- the old test documented the mismatch
  it was pinning. Updated to `selection_or_planning_exception`, with the reason
  recorded inline, so the two lines now agree.
- tests/python/test_arc_refactor_write_collapse_instrumentation_20260803.py
  guards the round-row key set, and `channel_chars` was undeclared. Added to
  `_SIBLING_REQ_ROW_KEYS`. That guard did its job; I had not run it.

THE REAL BUG: the widening created the mis-attribution in reverse. The no-plan
fall-through at the loop tail was the ONE exit that never assigned `skipped`, so
an earlier round's dynamics failure survived into an attempt that ended on the
planner. Concretely: round 1 fails held-out verification, rounds 2-3 VERIFY and
fail only at planning, and the attempt reported a dynamics failure. Latent at the
shipped MAX_REFINEMENT_ROUNDS=1, live whenever the cap is raised -- which the
REQ's own test fixture and several experiment scripts do. The fall-through now
claims its cause, so the semantics are last-round-wins throughout.

THREE MORE FINDINGS, ALL REAL.

- The loop-side `channels_before` read was DECORATIVE: replacing it with `{}`
  makes every round publish the whole-run cumulative total -- precisely the
  failure M7 claims to guard -- and the suite stayed GREEN. M7 only tested the
  delta helper in isolation, and every integration test used a proposer with no
  counters, so `channel_chars` was `{}` throughout. Now covered by a proposer
  that actually accumulates.
- `_round_digest` head-sliced and dropped the LAST round, which is the round
  whose cause the attempt reports. The digest could assert a cause and show no
  evidence for it -- this REQ's own failure mode one layer down. The same cap
  discarded the exception counterexample, which is appended last and exists
  nowhere else, defeating the stated reason for keeping both views. Now keeps
  head and tail.
- The harness `_channel_delta` had no clamp, despite SCENARIO-6710-7 requiring
  one, and returned -500 on a counter reset. It also runs AFTER the episode, so
  raising on a junk value would destroy a whole row of real data over a
  diagnostic field. Clamped and made junk-tolerant. The harness also read
  `proposer.channel_totals` defensively at entry and bare at exit; both are
  defensive now.

MUTATION PROOFS. Four new mutations, each RED, each restored byte-identical:

  M8  `channels_before = {}` (loop-side read removed)          RED 1 failed
  M9  no-plan fall-through no longer claims its cause          RED 1 failed
  M10 `_keep_head_and_tail` reverts to a plain head-slice      RED 1 failed
  M11 harness delta reverts to unclamped                       RED 1 failed

CORRECTED FIGURE. The "9 of 18 skip records" I took from the originating brief
does not reproduce. Sweeping every `induction_skipped` counter under `results/**`
on 2026-08-24: the default is 9 of 120 skip records outside the
induction-disabled case, and 9 of 3034 including it. The numerator reproduces;
the denominator does not. Corrected in the spec, ops/status.md, ops/changelog.md
and the test prose, with the provenance stated rather than the number restated.

ops/status.md also cited a second agent's test file by a name that no longer
exists -- it was renamed mid-session. Corrected to the current name and marked
as that agent's work.

VERIFICATION, done properly this time. Every suite that references
`arc_llm_reinduction`, `arc_scored_path_lever_harness`,
`execute_bounded_llm_reinduction`, `LocalGGUFProposer`, `channel_totals` or
`_round_digest` -- 85 suites, 1223 tests. 1206 pass, 17 fail. All 17 failures
reproduce identically at 288ea485f9~1 in a clean detached worktree, so they are
pre-existing and untouched by this work; they concern the defect gate, code-only
induce scoping, induce split fallback, a model-pin assertion and run-stop
authority. The worktree was removed afterwards.

tests/python/test_arc_induction_diagnosis_6710_invariants.py is another agent's
concurrent work on the same three defects. They staged it; it is included here
rather than unstaged, so it is not lost, and the authorship is theirs.

TEST-RUN MUTATION MARKERS DELETED DELIBERATELY, per the guard's own documented
resolution for an intended change. Three markers were pending; one was armed by
